0,0],[7,7,4,7,7,0,7,7,7,7,7,0,7,7,4,7,7],[4,4,4,4,4,0,7,7,7,7,7,0,4,4,4,4,4],[7,7,4,7,7,0,7,7,7,7,7,0,7,7,4,7,7],[7,4,7,4,7,0,7,7,7,7,7,0,7,4,7,4,7],[4,7,7,7,4,0,7,7,7,7,7,0,4,7,7,7,4]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"## How the puzzle works\n\n**What the grid is made of.** In every grid, full rows and columns of colour 0 split the canvas into equal panels. The panel interior is background 7. Two kinds of special content appear inside the panels:\n\n- **One pattern panel.** It holds a motif in a colour that is neither 0 nor the background:\n  - pair 1: the 9-coloured \"S/hook\" shape in the panel at rows 12–16, cols 12–16;\n  - pair 2: the vertical 2-line in the top-left panel.\n- **Marker panels.** Several other panels contain a single stray 0 cell.\n\n**What changes.** Compare input and output:\n\n- Pair 1 has five stray 0 dots, at (2,8), (8,8), (14,20), (20,2) and (20,20). In the output, each panel that contained a dot now holds an exact copy of the 9-motif. The motif sits at the same offset inside the panel as in the source panel, and the dot itself is gone (it was overwritten).\n- The fact sheet confirms this. It lists five new 9-objects of size 8, each the same shape as the original, sitting exactly in those panels.\n- The only other transitions are 0→7 and 7→9, which matches \"the dot panel is replaced wholesale by the pattern panel\".\n- Pair 2 behaves the same way. The dots at (5,5), (9,5) and (9,9) mark three panels, and each gets the 2-line copied into it.\n- Panels without a dot are left untouched.\n\n**Rule.**\n1. Find the panels between the 0 dividers.\n2. The pattern panel is the one containing a colour other than the background and 0.\n3. Every panel that contains a 0 cell inside it is overwritten with a copy of the pattern panel.\n\n**Test input.**\n- The 17×17 grid has dividers at rows/cols 5 and 11, giving a 3×3 arrangement of 5×5 panels.\n- The pattern panel is the top-right one, which holds the 4-coloured figure.\n- Dots sit at (8,8) in the centre panel, (14,2) in the bottom-left panel and (14,14) in the bottom-right panel.\n- Each of those three panels receives the 4-figure.\n\n**Construction stages.** The program first copies the input. It then emits one stage per marked panel, as that panel is overwritten by the pattern. Finally it emits the finished grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    boxes = panels(g)\n    # locate the pattern panel: contains a colour other than bg and 0\n    pat = None\n    for (y0, x0, y1, x1) in boxes:\n        sub = g[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1]\n        if np.any((sub != bg) & (sub != 0)):\n            pat = sub.copy()\n            break\n    if pat is None:\n        emit(out, \"No pattern panel found; grid unchanged.\")\n        return out\n    ph, pw = pat.shape\n    for (y0, x0, y1, x1) in boxes:\n        sub = g[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1]\n        if sub.shape != (ph, pw):\n            continue\n        if np.any(sub == 0):\n            out[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1] = pat\n            emit(out, f\"Panel at rows {y0}-{y1}, cols {x0}-{x1} contained a 0 marker, \"\n                      f\"so it is replaced by a copy of the pattern panel.\")\n    emit(out, \"All marked panels now hold the pattern; final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"the grid is made of.** In every grid, full rows and columns of colour 0 split the canvas into equal panels."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The panel interior is background 7."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Two kinds of special content appear inside the panels:"}],"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"It lists five new 9-objects of size 8, each the same shape as the original, sitting exactly in those panels."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **One pattern panel.** It holds a motif in a colour that is neither 0 nor the background:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In the output, each panel that contained a dot now holds an exact copy of the 9-motif."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The motif sits at the same offset inside the panel as in the source panel, and the dot itself is gone (it was overwritten)."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The panel interior is background 7."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"cc3ebcf03bc23efc59a3d365caf7d09ff6f1bf1e56727f76975c8552f52254cd","task_sha256":"d90be8b640fa3a7ec8a3255e9a3b539ea54c1a5a3468f1b510a696fabbbc4db5","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
